From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:23:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/72] test: build drift-suite fixtures line-by-line, not with
 embedded escapes (gcp-co9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Carried over from 857ba86 on the pre-rebase branch, whose other half is now
redundant. That commit fixed two regressions from the prompt-drift change; only
one of them is still live on integration.

The dropped half excluded patches/ from tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py.
dabcb2c (gcp-xbl) landed the same exclusion independently as DERIVED_PREFIXES
while this branch was held, so replaying ours would only re-implement it in a
second style. Integration's version is kept.

The half that survives is this one: the new drift suite built its detector
self-test fixtures with embedded "\n" escapes, and a literal backslash-n
immediately before `gc` reads as a bare `bd` invocation to
test_no_bare_bd_commands.py, whose gc-prefix check is line-based. Nothing on
integration fixes that — the fixtures only exist on this branch — so without
this the bare-bd guard fails against our own new test file. Rebuilt with
"\n".join(...) so each command starts a line.
---
 tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py | 28 +++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py b/tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py
index f798183..133fbb3 100644
--- a/tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py
+++ b/tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py
@@ -222,16 +222,28 @@ def test_detectors_catch_the_drift_they_are_named_for() -> None:
         fixture, 'gc bd update $WORK --status=open --assignee="$REFINERY_TARGET"'
     )
 
-    unguarded_warrant = (
-        "```bash\ngc bd create --type=task --label=warrant "
-        "--metadata '{\"target\":\"x\"}'\n```"
+    # Built line-by-line rather than with embedded "\n" escapes: a literal
+    # backslash-n immediately before `gc` reads as a bare `bd` invocation to
+    # tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py, whose gc-prefix check is line-based.
+    unguarded_warrant = "\n".join(
+        [
+            "```bash",
+            "gc bd create --type=task --label=warrant --metadata '{\"target\":\"x\"}'",
+            "```",
+        ]
     )
     assert warrant_dedup_violations(fixture, unguarded_warrant)
-    guarded_warrant = (
-        "```bash\nEXISTING_WARRANT=$(gc bd list --label=warrant --json)\n"
-        "if [ \"$EXISTING_WARRANT\" -gt 0 ]; then\n  echo skip\nelse\n"
-        "  gc bd create --type=task --label=warrant --metadata '{\"target\":\"x\"}'\n"
-        "fi\n```"
+    guarded_warrant = "\n".join(
+        [
+            "```bash",
+            "EXISTING_WARRANT=$(gc bd list --label=warrant --json)",
+            'if [ "$EXISTING_WARRANT" -gt 0 ]; then',
+            "  echo skip",
+            "else",
+            "  gc bd create --type=task --label=warrant --metadata '{\"target\":\"x\"}'",
+            "fi",
+            "```",
+        ]
     )
     assert not warrant_dedup_violations(fixture, guarded_warrant)
     # A quick-reference table row is outside any fenced block, so it can never
